WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.240
Who doesn’t love a walk through a dark forest? The&nbsp;
sight of branches set against the low moonlight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.440
looking like all manner of dark and twisted&nbsp;
claws reaching out of the night to grab at you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.280
Every step brings with it the snap of a broken&nbsp;
twig that practically echoes around you. Whenever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:23.840
a breeze rustles the leaves on the trees, you feel&nbsp;
like something might just be following you, moving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.920
through the forest towards you. It’s easy to get&nbsp;
lost in a forest at night, after all, that’s why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:36.880
the children’s song warns us that “if you go down&nbsp;
to the woods today, you’d better not go alone.”&nbsp;

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:43.040
The image of a forest in the darkness has inspired&nbsp;
fear for generations, from fireside folktales&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.320
telling of wolves and monsters lurking among&nbsp;
the trees, to modern horror games about a tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:55.760
faceless man in a suit stalking you through the&nbsp;
woods. And then, of course, there’s SCP-060,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:03.760
otherwise known as the Infernal Occult Skeleton.
Now, despite its name, SCP-060 is, in actual fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.600
a forest. Or at least, it’s a forest to begin&nbsp;
with. A picturesque grove of seventeen tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:16.000
white oak trees, spread out across eight acres&nbsp;
of land in rural northeast Minnesota. It almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.560
looks like something out of a tourist brochure,&nbsp;
a beautiful stretch of forest sitting under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:26.640
clear skies, well, during the daytime anyway.
If you ever find yourself hiking through a corner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:32.160
of Minnesotan forest that isn’t in any of the&nbsp;
guidebooks, then tread carefully. You might just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:39.040
stumble upon the demolished ruins of a house that&nbsp;
used to stand among the trees, out in seclusion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:45.760
And a word of advice to you if you happen across&nbsp;
this place, do not, under any circumstances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.080
stop walking for a smoke break.
Of course, thanks to the good folks at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:57.360
the SCP Foundation, you’re unlikely to ever just&nbsp;
wander your way into SCP-060. More likely, they’ll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:03.040
administer you with amnestics – the Foundation’s&nbsp;
patented memory-altering drugs – and send you on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:10.160
your merry way, totally oblivious to the huge,&nbsp;
hard-to-miss greenhouses containing SCP-060.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:14.880
Beyond those glass walls, you might have caught&nbsp;
glimpses of Foundation personnel watering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:22.480
trees, carefully tending to each SCP-060 specimen.
Maybe you saw them gathering up leaves and pruning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.760
each tree individually, composting every part of&nbsp;
dead plant matter instead of leaving the white&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.960
oaks to grow freely. And perhaps you even&nbsp;
noticed that not one member of personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:39.440
was carrying a lighter on their person, nor a&nbsp;
taser, or so much as a small box of matches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:44.640
nothing that can start a fire. Or rather,&nbsp;
you would remember seeing all that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:50.880
if the amnestics hadn’t already made you forget.
But what’s so special about these trees? Why would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:56.240
the SCP Foundation go to the extent of housing&nbsp;
a collection of white oaks in greenhouses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:01.600
and meticulously oversee their growth? What&nbsp;
is it about these particular specimens that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:10.480
make personnel so cautious about fire safety? And&nbsp;
why on earth is SCP-060, a collection of trees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.800
referred to by the nickname&nbsp;
‘the Infernal Occult Skeleton’?&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.480
Well, the answer to all those questions&nbsp;
becomes pretty apparent the moment any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:26.000
of the SCP-060 oak trees catch fire, and&nbsp;
something comes hurtling out of the forest.&nbsp;

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.920
That something is known as SCP-060-Alpha.&nbsp;
Standing at just over two meters tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.880
the entity takes the form of an adult human&nbsp;
skeleton. Much more than just a spooky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:43.280
scary collection of bones, SCP-060-Alpha is&nbsp;
fully animate, capable of moving of its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:49.760
accord without the aid of muscles or a nervous&nbsp;
system. Oh, and it also happens to be on fire.&nbsp;

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:56.960
Move aside Ghost Rider, SCP-060-Alpha is engulfed&nbsp;
from skull to toe bones in bright white flames,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:01.760
burning at a temperature of approximately&nbsp;
fifteen-hundred degrees Celsius, or almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:07.040
three thousand degrees Fahrenheit. For reference,&nbsp;
that’s just shy of the melting point of iron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.920
and hot enough to grant a human being&nbsp;
a quick, but agonizingly painful death.&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.400
Granted after a few seconds of that heat your&nbsp;
nerve endings would be scalded, so maybe you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.760
wouldn’t feel that much pain. But fifteen-hundred&nbsp;
Celsius is enough to burn the moisture right out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:27.200
of your skin, melt your eyeballs, and generally&nbsp;
fry you to a crisp in a matter of minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:33.600
if not seconds. Good thing SCP-060-Alpha isn’t&nbsp;
known for being highly aggressive and hostile.&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.280
Oh, wait, it is? Ah, not good.&nbsp;

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:42.320
Upon manifestation, the burning skeleton will&nbsp;
attempt to do as much damage as possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:47.600
and usually to whoever is closest. It can appear&nbsp;
at any time, and after as little as twenty grams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:53.520
worth of one of the SCP-060 trees is burned.&nbsp;
As if being actively hostile and burning hot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:59.280
enough to reshape metal wasn’t bad enough,&nbsp;
SCP-060-Alpha has also shown itself to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:04.800
fiercely intelligent. The entity seems to retain&nbsp;
knowledge whenever it manifests and has gained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:11.360
a growing familiarity with the layout of the&nbsp;
Foundation site that contains the SCP-060 oaks.&nbsp;

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.680
The Infernal Occult Skeleton’s methods of attack&nbsp;
tend to include throwing its entire body at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:22.480
flammable materials; however, it will avoid&nbsp;
causing any damage to specimens of SCP-060.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:27.120
The skeletal entity can run at speeds of up&nbsp;
to fifty miles per hour, now that’s almost the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:33.040
same speed as a gazelle. Just picturing anything&nbsp;
traveling towards you at that speed is horrifying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:38.160
let alone something heading straight for you&nbsp;
at gazelle levels of speed while also on fire!&nbsp;

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:44.640
It’s this combination of speed and heat that means&nbsp;
SCP-060-Alpha poses such a threat to anyone close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:49.520
whenever it appears; if left unchecked,&nbsp;
the entity could easily cause colossal and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:55.680
widespread forest fires and property damage.
Interestingly, any areas that SCP-060-Alpha&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.120
does burn with its flames, will start&nbsp;
to yield saplings of the SCP-060 oaks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:06.000
around six weeks after the fire has stopped. The&nbsp;
Foundation doesn’t allow these saplings to grow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.880
to full size, and instead pulls them from the&nbsp;
ground and disposes of them, composting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:18.160
saplings to feed the other SCP-060 specimens.
Luckily, the biggest strength of SCP-060-Alpha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:23.440
its flames, also happens to be its greatest&nbsp;
weakness. It is possible to fight the fires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:28.000
of the Infernal Occult Skeleton by dousing&nbsp;
it with water or any other materials capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:32.960
of dousing flames, whether it’s sand or&nbsp;
foam from a fire extinguisher. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:38.240
this is a lot hotter and harder to put out than&nbsp;
any ordinary, smaller-scale fire, but despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:44.640
being a difficult task, it’s not impossible. About&nbsp;
five hundred liters of water should do the trick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:50.240
if you’ve got a big enough bucket nearby.
After that, SCP-060-Alpha will be weakened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:56.000
gradually collapsing and turning into dust.&nbsp;
However, if another part of an SCP-060 tree is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:01.200
burned and the entity reappears, it is believed&nbsp;
that this will be the same Infernal Occult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:06.960
Skeleton, rather than a new version of the bone&nbsp;
burning being. So, we have a grove of oak trees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.600
that manifest a flaming skeleton if they are ever&nbsp;
burned. Maybe that’s not the weirdest thing you’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:17.120
see in a Minnesotan forest, but wait, there’s&nbsp;
something else. Cast your mind back a few minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:22.080
and you’ll remember that we mentioned some ruins,&nbsp;
the remains of a demolished house that used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:28.640
stand secluded among the SCP-060 white oak trees.
Knowing that the Infernal Occult Skeleton can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.080
appear from the oaks might make it&nbsp;
obvious what happened to this house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.800
but there’s still a story to be told here.
The house’s owner was a man by the name of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:43.040
Johnathan Corhill. Now, Johnathan was something&nbsp;
of an odd man, considered a bit of an eccentric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:48.720
to some. He preferred to spend his time in&nbsp;
solitude, alone with his own thoughts for company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.200
rather than mingling among the rest of the&nbsp;
world. Even his own family noticed that Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:58.480
Corhill was drifting away from them, becoming a&nbsp;
more bitter, nihilistic person in his old age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:04.080
and choosing isolation over human connection.&nbsp;
Now, sure, loneliness doesn’t hold much appeal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:08.560
to everyone, but sometimes there are&nbsp;
people who just prefer being alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:14.080
That might be what drew Johnathan Corhill to his&nbsp;
secluded little house in the forests of Minnesota,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.920
somewhere no one would bother him.
For the most part, the rest of the Corhill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:22.800
family adjusted to their eccentric relative’s&nbsp;
behavior. Johnathan would have rarely accepted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:28.240
visitors to his house in the forest, but he still&nbsp;
kept in contact with those he’d been close with.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:32.800
Most notably, he’d regularly share phone&nbsp;
calls with his brother, one Christopher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:40.320
Corhill. That is... Until something seemed&nbsp;
to change unexpectedly, in the year 1996.&nbsp;

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:44.880
On one of their calls, Johnathan outright&nbsp;
told Christopher to never contact him again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:49.840
severing all ties with any remaining family&nbsp;
members and friends in the outside world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:54.560
Johnathan cut everyone off, living within his&nbsp;
own bubble where he could immerse himself in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.560 --> 00:09:00.160
his unusual interests. According to Christopher,&nbsp;
his brother had seemed otherwise normal up until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.520
a certain phone conversation, but Johnathan had&nbsp;
become obsessed with the occult. Specifically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.960
he had embroiled himself in the history of the&nbsp;
Victorian-era, and certain supernatural practices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:15.680
that had been undertaken in that time period.
Now whether Christopher honored his brother’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:21.360
wish to sever ties is unknown. A mail carrier&nbsp;
would visit Johnathan’s home in the woods not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:26.240
long after their phone call. Maybe among the&nbsp;
envelopes, this courier was delivering what could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:31.040
have been a letter from Christopher, or other&nbsp;
members of the Corhill family, begging their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:36.000
estranged relative to come back to the world.&nbsp;
You see, even people who claim to prefer being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.360
on their own sometimes need human interaction.&nbsp;
Talking to people, being in the presence of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:46.880
friends and family, are hugely important factors&nbsp;
in maintaining a positive state of mental health.&nbsp;

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:51.520
But what happens when someone rejects that&nbsp;
entirely and instead becomes lost in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:56.720
obsessive study of the occult? Well, the&nbsp;
mail carrier was the first to find out.&nbsp;

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:01.440
Arriving at Johnathan Corhill’s woodland&nbsp;
house, the courier found the place looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:07.200
almost skeletal, a shell of the building that had&nbsp;
once stood in the forest. According to the locals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.240
the carrier had been sent to deliver a notice to&nbsp;
Mr Corhill, explaining that his house was being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:19.440
foreclosed. But it seemed someone, or something,&nbsp;
had beaten them to it. A fire had spread from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:26.560
house’s fireplace, quickly engulfing the entire&nbsp;
structure, presumably with Johnathan still inside.&nbsp;

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.480
It wasn’t until later that very same year&nbsp;
that Johnathan Corhill was officially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:35.920
reported as a missing person case with local&nbsp;
authorities. Any search that was undertaken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:40.960
in an attempt to find him uncovered&nbsp;
next to no evidence of his whereabouts.&nbsp;

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:46.320
To this day, nobody knows for certain if&nbsp;
Johnathan Corhill is dead or alive, his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:51.760
whereabouts are unknown. On the surface, it might&nbsp;
be easy to make the assumption that the Infernal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:57.760
Occult Skeleton reduced the reclusive old man to&nbsp;
nothing more than a cinder. It definitely seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:02.880
plausible that Johnathan, collecting firewood to&nbsp;
keep himself warm in his isolation, accidentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:09.920
chopped down part of an SCP-060 oak, put it in his&nbsp;
fireplace, and called forth the vengeful flaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:16.720
bones. But perhaps we shouldn’t be so certain.
After all, Corhill’s house wasn’t entirely burned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:22.640
down, despite the entity normally trying to cause&nbsp;
as much damage as possible whenever it appears.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:29.520
And on top of that, no human remains were found&nbsp;
in the house. And the skeleton of SCP-060-Alpha&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:36.080
had to have come from somewhere, right?
SCP-060 offers a few warnings, and not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:40.800
about the dangers of traveling through the forest&nbsp;
alone. The appearance of the flaming skeleton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:46.160
whenever the SCP-060 white oaks are burned&nbsp;
could serve as a reminder that we need to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:52.080
vigilant in protecting the forests of this world.&nbsp;
Trees are one of our few sustainable resources,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:58.240
but for every one we cut down or that catches&nbsp;
fire, it takes years to regrow a replacement.&nbsp;

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:03.040
And perhaps the third and final warning&nbsp;
of the Infernal Occult Skeleton is simply:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:08.960
don’t play with matches, especially around&nbsp;
trees. Otherwise, you might get burned.&nbsp;

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:15.360
Now go check out “The Plane That Never Was&nbsp;
SCP-787” and “SCP 1440 - The Old Man That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:19.840
Kills All Living Things He Touches”&nbsp;
for more morbidly fascinating SCPs!

